 "notes": "Table XV Part II (Bi-lingualism) concld.; continues from leaf 258. Records with subsidiary=null are 'Number of persons speaking mother tongue' (cols 18-19, 26-27). Only Males/Females printed; persons null. No division subtotals printed. Checks: Tibeto-Burmese speakers Males add exactly to the printed Total 807,190 (Lakhimpur read 27,601; its tens digit is a broken 0 of the same broken shape as other 0s on the page). Tibeto-Burmese speakers Females: the other districts add to 771,903, so the printed Total 813,904 implies Nowgong 42,001; the printed Nowgong figure reads 36,001 or 86,001 (first digit ambiguous) - recorded '?'. Lakhimpur Females tens digit is broken (read 23,683). Tibeto-Burmese MT / Assamese subsidiary Males: districts add to 75,695; printed Total read 75,698 (italic, last digit 8 or 5 - kept as read). Females reconcile (49,928). Tibeto-Burmese MT / Bengali and Khasi-Synteng subsidiary: reconcile. Khasi-Synteng speakers: reconcile with printed Total and agree with Part I Khasi (Khasi States Males 74,443 has broken 4s). Khasi-Synteng MT / Tibeto-Burmese subsidiary Females: districts add to 74 (Khasi and Jaintia Hills 44 and Lushai Hills 23, both smudged), printed Total 73; kept as read. Other Khasi-Synteng subsidiary columns reconcile."
